    {
      "id": "US-276",
      "title": "Add epic-level hierarchical orchestration with supervisor worker and DAG dispatch",
      "priority": "low",
      "description": "Large epics in prd.json have no structural relationship to their child stories; a single orchestrator dispatches all stories without priority awareness within an epic. A hierarchical orchestration mode assigns one supervisor worker per epic that reads the dependency graph, orders sub-stories topologically, and dispatches sub-workers in sequence or parallel — matching the NeurIPS 2025 finding that learned task routing outperforms fixed pipelines by structuring work before distributing it.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "prd.json stories gain an optional _epicId field; stories sharing an _epicId form an epic group",
        "When SPIRAL_HIERARCHICAL_MODE=true, spiral.sh creates one supervisor process per epic before dispatching sub-workers",
        "The supervisor builds a dependency DAG from stories' dependencies[] fields using topological sort and dispatches sub-workers in dependency order",
        "Sub-worker progress is reported back to the supervisor, which updates the epic-level status in prd.json",
        "If a sub-worker fails, the supervisor applies existing dead-letter queue logic and continues dispatching independent stories in the epic",
        "spiral status shows epics as collapsible groups with aggregate progress displayed as 'X/N stories done'"
      ],
      "technicalNotes": [
        "NeurIPS 2025 dynamic orchestration: learned task routing outperforms fixed multi-agent pipelines — https://blog.promptlayer.com/multi-agent-evolving-orchestration/",
        "Orchestrator-Worker pattern: https://gurusup.com/blog/agent-orchestration-patterns — central coordinator with fan-out to workers",
        "Topological sort: Python graphlib.TopologicalSorter (stdlib, Python 3.9+) for the dependency DAG",
        "Supervisor state persisted to .spiral/workers/<epic-id>/supervisor_state.json for crash recovery"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "estimatedComplexity": "large",
      "passes": false
    },
