      "id": "US-282",
      "title": "Semantic near-duplicate story detection using sentence-transformer embeddings",
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "Augment the existing title-similarity deduplication in merge_stories.py with vector-embedding-based semantic deduplication. Two stories whose embeddings have cosine similarity >= 0.92 are flagged as near-duplicates and the lower-priority one is rejected, even when their titles differ substantially.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "merge_stories.py computes embeddings for new story titles+descriptions using sentence-transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
        "Stories with cosine similarity >= 0.92 against any existing prd.json story are logged as duplicates and dropped from the merge batch",
        "Embedding computation is optional: if sentence-transformers is not installed, falls back to existing title-comparison logic with a warning",
        "Unit test verifies that two paraphrased stories (same intent, different wording) are deduplicated",
        "Embedding cache is persisted to .spiral/embed_cache.pkl to avoid recomputation on every iteration"
      ],
      "technicalNotes": [
        "Use sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (22 MB, fast CPU inference) via pip installable package",
        "Cosine similarity threshold 0.92-0.95 catches near-duplicates with low false-positive rate per SemDedup research",
        "For PRDs > 500 stories, use FAISS IndexFlatIP for O(log n) ANN search instead of O(n^2) pairwise",
        "Reference: NVIDIA SemDedup technique: https://docs.nvidia.com/nemo-framework/user-guide/latest/datacuration/semdedup.html"
