    {
      "id": "US-283",
      "title": "Automated git bisect on Phase V failure to locate regression-introducing commit",
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "When Phase V validation fails and SPIRAL_BISECT_ON_FAILURE=true is set, automatically run `git bisect run` using SPIRAL_VALIDATE_CMD as the test script. The bisect result (offending commit SHA) is written to .spiral/_bisect_result.json and displayed in the dashboard.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "When Phase V returns non-zero and SPIRAL_BISECT_ON_FAILURE=true, spiral.sh runs git bisect start HEAD <last_known_good_sha>",
        "git bisect run is invoked with a wrapper script that executes SPIRAL_VALIDATE_CMD; exit 0 = good, exit 1 = bad, exit 125 = skip",
        "_bisect_result.json is written with fields: offending_sha, commit_message, story_id, timestamp",
        "Bisect aborts cleanly (git bisect reset) whether it succeeds or times out via SPIRAL_BISECT_TIMEOUT_MINUTES",
        "If no known-good SHA is available in _checkpoint.json, bisect is skipped with a warning"
      ],
      "technicalNotes": [
        "git bisect run <script> exits 0 when bisect identifies the first bad commit; the commit SHA is in git bisect log output",
        "Bisect test scripts must exit 125 to skip untestable commits (e.g., build failures); this is different from exit 1 (definitively bad)",
        "Store last known-good SHA as _lastGoodSha in .spiral/_checkpoint.json after each successful Phase V",
        "Reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-bisect — 'git bisect run' section"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
